{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he brought near to his brothers the Midianite woman.</b> It would have been fitting for Scripture to say: 'And behold, a man came whose name was Zimri, prince of a father's house of the Shimonites, and he brought near to his brothers the Midianite woman, and her name was Cozbi daughter of Zur.' But Scripture did not wish to mention this wicked man by name, for he was the cause of the plague, until vengeance was executed upon him and until Pinhas was given his reward — and only then does Scripture mention them by name: 'and the name of the slain Israelite man…' and 'and the name of the slain woman…' And this is to inform us of Pinhas's praise, that even though this one was a prince and this one a king's daughter, he did not refrain from killing them." "<b>In the sight of Mosheh and in the sight of all the congregation of the children of Israel.</b> He showed no respect for Heaven and no respect for creatures." "<b>And they were weeping.</b> The children of Israel were weeping because of the plague, for the wrath of HaShem had begun among them. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted that they were weeping because a halakhah was concealed from Mosheh — for Zimri said to her, 'Listen to me.' She said to him, 'I do not listen to you but to Mosheh and to Elazar, for I am a king's daughter.' He said to her, 'I am as great as they are; before their eyes I bring you in.' He seized her by her forelock and brought her before Mosheh. He said to him, 'Son of Amram, is this one forbidden or permitted? If you say forbidden — the daughter of Yitro, who permitted her to you?' Immediately the halakhah was concealed from him. They all burst into weeping — that is what is written: ״והמה בוכים״, at the entrance of the tent of meeting. Why 'weeping'? And can it enter your mind that Mosheh's hands were weak — he who stood against sixty myriads, as it is said (Exodus 32:20): ״ויקח את העגל אשר עשו וישרוף באש״? Rather, so that Pinhas would come and take his reward. And concerning this it is said (Proverbs 30:31): ״זרזיר מתנים או תיש״, and our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted it of Zimri; and 'a king' — this is Mosheh, who had no answer against him, because the halakhah was concealed from him."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:04.059183331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}